{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T15:20:45.143Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"877aec11872ca473544699e2","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"**Version:** 2026.10.23. **Scope:** core exported runTemplatesSave and option typing. Medium correctness / extension-author UX.\n\nRun via npx -y tsx in a fresh scratch npm project containing the pinned SDK. The current directory must be a fresh scratch workspace; use an ESM filename such as repro.mts:\n\n~~~ts\nimport { PmClient, runTemplatesSave } from '@unbrained/pm-cli';\nconst c = new PmClient({ cwd: process.cwd(), author: 'codex-agent' });\nawait c.init(undefined, { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip' });\nawait c.packageInstall('templates');\nconst g = { path: process.cwd() + '/.agents/pm', author: 'codex-agent' };\nconst direct = await c.create({ type: 'Task', title: 'Direct', priority: 0 });\nconst saved = await runTemplatesSave('numeric', { type: 'Task', priority: 0 }, g);\nconst item = await c.create({ template: 'numeric', title: 'From numeric' });\nawait runTemplatesSave('string', { type: 'Task', priority: '0' }, g);\nconst control = await c.create({ template: 'string', title: 'From string' });\nconsole.log(direct.item.priority, saved.options, item.item.priority,\n  control.item.priority);\n~~~\n\n**Observed:** strict TypeScript accepts numeric priority because save takes Record<string, unknown>. Output is **0, {type:'Task'}, 2, 0**. Direct numeric creation works; saving removes priority without warning/rejection; template creation receives default priority 2; string-priority control works. The independent tiny tracker agrees with the larger fixture. A misspelled prority key is also accepted/persisted, an ancillary typing observation.\n\n**Expected:** publish supported template-save option types and normalize valid numeric priority, or reject unsupported values before saving with an actionable error. If this API intentionally accepts strings only, constrain its signature accordingly. Accepting unknown inputs and silently deleting values is the narrow defect; arbitrary unknown objects need not be preserved.\n\n**Measured cost:** compact SDK save receipt **197 bytes / 49.25 tokens**, with priority already absent and no diagnostic. Wrong-priority create receipt **448 bytes / 112 tokens**. Save+create uses **two calls / 161.25 tokens**, still without a mismatch diagnostic. The five-call direct/numeric/string controls cost **443.5 compact SDK tokens**. Workaround: stringify priority explicitly.\n\n**Duplicate searches**, same all-state limit-20 command:\n\n- \"templates\" \"SDK\"\n- \"templates\" \"priority\"\n- \"templates\" \"unknown\"\n- \"runTemplatesSave\"\n- template numeric priority\n- template number dropped\n\n#497 was read: it concerns applying stored tags/custom type-option fields during create, where stored built-in priority applied. This draft concerns discarding a numeric built-in value at the public save boundary before storage. #439 is the broad execution surface. No matching save-boundary report found.\n\n\n\n---\nFound by an agent-UX probe of 2026.10.23 (agent seat and extension-author seat) and re-verified by the maintainer orchestrator against the globally installed 2026.10.23 before filing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1561"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1561: normalize numeric template-save priority and publish supported options"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported on2026.10.23: public runTemplatesSave accepts numeric priority0 via Record<string, unknown> but silently omits it, so a later templated item receives priority2. The string0 control and direct numeric create work. Investigate typed save options and pre-write normalization/refusal."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1561","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-23T15:20:45.143Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T15:20:45.143Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-780f"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Supported numeric template priorities survive save/create or unsupported inputs are rejected actionably before saving; the public SDK option type documents accepted values."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.10.23"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-23T15:20:45.143Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Intake source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1561. Duplicate checks: request-specific live PM search, fresh open/in_progress lists and complete3080-item strict all-status read, with no omissions; full live parent comments/closure and verified complete history were inspected. The report is distinct from the delivered parent scope. Intake only: not independently reproduced in this delivery, open and unclaimed; preserve completed parent history."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2359b0e479451af23d1a71f031cd8523b9d97afd8097d7897745e6cedba5c9ea","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"c